# Commands Learnt

- sqrt()
  Header: <cmath>
  Use: Square root
  Syntax: sqrt(number)
  Example: sqrt(25) → 5
  Important: Returns float/double value
  Source: HackerRank (Point Distance Problem)

- pow()
  Header: <cmath>
  Use: Power of a number
  Syntax: pow(base, exponent)
  Example: pow(2,3) → 8
  Important: Returns float/double value
  Source: HackerRank (Point Distance Problem)

- fixed
  Header: <iomanip>
  Use: Prints numbers in decimal format
  Example: cout << fixed << 3.14159265359;
  Output: 3.141593
  Important:
    • Default = 6 digits after decimal
    • Usually used with setprecision()
  Source: HackerRank (Data Types)

- setprecision()
  Header: <iomanip>
  Use: Controls precision of output
  Syntax: setprecision(n)
  Example:
    setprecision(3) → 3 significant digits
    fixed << setprecision(3) → 3 digits after decimal
  Important:
    • Alone → controls significant digits
    • With fixed → controls digits after decimal
  Source: HackerRank (Data Types)

- string.length()
  Header: <string>
  Use: Find length of string
  Syntax: string_name.length()
  Example: "hello".length() → 5
  Important: Returns number of characters
  Source: Analyzing Other Programs (Binary Number Program)

- string.at()
  Header: <string>
  Use: Access character at a specific index
  Syntax: string_name.at(index)
  Example: "hello".at(1) → e
  Important: Index starts from 0
  Source: Analyzing Other Programs (Binary Number Program)